  "headline": "Sigiriya & Dambulla: Sky Citadels, Water Gardens & Gilded Cave Sanctuaries",
  "description": "At the heart of the Cultural Triangle, a 200-metre granite monolith rises out of the dry-zone forest, crowned by the ruins of King Kashyapa’s fifth-century sky palace. Below it lie symmetrical water gardens, mirror walls and the celebrated cloud-maiden frescoes.\n\nTwenty kilometres away, the Dambulla cave temples hold more than two thousand years of devotion in five painted chambers. I pair both with quiet evenings at Kandalama reservoir and village kitchens where lunch is still cooked in clay over wood embers.",
